             :intent "`(dir my.program)` at an agent's REPL lists `my.program/supplied-context` (`:seon.fn/internal? true`) and arglists carrying supplied members (`my.program/source` as `[database sym]`), so bench agents passed them by hand: `(my.program/source (my.program/supplied-context {}) 'comp.geo/area)` and `(my.program/diff (my.program/supplied-context nil))` gave 8 refusals across 65 runs (bench E0-E1, 2026-10-09). Done when `dir` omits internal functions and shows each arglist as the agent calls it, without supplied world members."
